      "title": "Management of Information Systems Professor (open rank)",
      "description": " Management of Information Systems Professor (open rank) at NovaSBE Position: Assistant, Associate Professor in Information Systems Starting date: September 1, 2027 Institution: Nova School of Business and Economics (Universidade Nova de Lisboa) Location: Lisbon, Portugal Position description: Nova School of Business and Economics (Nova SBE), a triple - accredited institution (AACSB, EQUIS , and AMBA), open s a position the Assistant or Associate (tenure track) Professor level in Management of Information Systems starting on September 1, 202 7. Applicants should have a Ph.D. degree in Management of Information Systems, Business Analytics, Computer Science or a related discipline by the start date. Applicants should exhibit a solid research record and need to demonstrate ability to publish in leading international business peer-reviewed journals , such as Management Science , Information Systems Research, and MIS Quarterly . Selected applicants are also expected to contribute to teaching in Management of Information Systems, Business Analytics, Data Management, Privacy, or other related areas. Compensation is competitive with top universities in Europe. School description: Nova SBE offers programs in management, economics, and finance at the undergraduate, master, MBA, and doctorate levels, as well as executive education. Nova SBE provides an international research environment and ranks consistently among the top business schools in Europe. To support the development of a research -oriented career, Nova SBE provides a balanced teaching workload , compensation, and research- support incentives that are competitive with top business schools in Europe. English is the working language of the school and knowledge of Portuguese is not a requirement. Nova SBE’s campus is in Lisbon at Carcavelos Beach. Lisbon is consistently ranked one of the cities with the best quality of life in the world and offers an outstanding combination of exceptional lifestyle, relatively low cost of living, and an extensive set of cultural and leisure opportunities. Application details: Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement and job market paper. Applications will be assessed on a rolling basis and candidates who submit their application package by October 1, 2026 will be given priority and considered for an interview during the annual INFORMS conference. All applications must be received by November 15, 202 6. Applications will be accepted online and must be submitted HERE (Qualtrics form). Referrers can send recommendation letters directly to faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt upon request. General details about working at Nova SBE to be found: JOIN OUR SCHOOL > Appointment of Professor of Management of Information Systems > Announcement Additional information can be obtained from: Faculty Affairs Department (faculty.affairs@novasbe.pt) Prof. Michail Batikas (michail.batikas@novasbe.pt) Prof. Rodrigo Belo (rodrigo.belo@novasbe.pt) Prof. Yufei Shen (yufei.shen@novasbe.pt) Info-EUREXESS The conditions of employment comply with the terms of Regulation no 409/2018 of 20 June, and the Labour Code, approved by Law no 7/2009 of 12 February, with subsequent amendments (\"Labour Code\"). Salary is subject to training and experience and may vary depending on the category (Assistant, Associate or Full) and career stage and based on a full -time contract of 35 hours. Favourable tax agreements may apply to non - Portuguese applicants. NovaSBE has attractive employment conditions, which include a holiday and Christmas allowance and a generous number of vacation days. "
